-- title:
--   Holomorphy of pull-backs of regular functions on edge-chart loci
-- statement:
--   The setting is a Čerednik–Drinfeld quotient datum together with an adic frame and a system of edge-chart morphisms; the hypotheses fall into the groups listed below, and every group is described.
--
--   **Base rings.** A prime $r$; a characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), with an irreducible element $\pi$, $\pi$-adically complete (`hcomplete`), whose residue ring $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements (`hres`) and for which $(r) = (\pi)$ as ideals of $\mathcal O$ (`hunr`); and a characteristic-zero field $K_0$ which is a fraction field of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **The unramified coefficient ring.** A characteristic-zero domain $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ over $\mathcal O$ with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, subject to: $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ (`hOnr_complete`); that ideal is maximal (`hOnr_max`); every element of $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ satisfies some monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`); every monic polynomial over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`); and $\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^{r} \pmod{\pi}$ for all $x$ (`hFr`).
--
--   **Valuation of the determinant.** A monoid homomorphism $v_{\det} : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) such that $v_{\det}(g) = n$ if and only if $\det g = u\,\pi^{n}$ in $K_0$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$ (`hvdet`).
--
--   **The group.** A group $G$, a homomorphism $\sigma : G \to \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$, a subgroup $\Gamma \le G$ containing an element $z$ with $\sigma z$ a scalar matrix $c\cdot 1$ and $v_{\det}(\sigma z) = 2$ (`hcent`) and an element $w$ with $v_{\det}(\sigma w) = 1$ (`hodd`), together with a subgroup $\Gamma'$ characterised by: $x \in \Gamma'$ iff $x \in \Gamma$ and $v_{\det}(\sigma x)$ is even (`hΓ'`). A homomorphism $\rho : G \to \mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ with $\rho g$ the class of $\sigma g$ (`hρ`), such that the image $\rho(\Gamma')$ has finite vertex stabilisers on the lattice tree $\mathrm{Vertex}\,\mathcal O\,K_0$ (`hdisc`) and finitely many orbits on its vertices (`hcocpt`).
--
--   **The quotient scheme and its functor of nilpotent points.** A scheme $\mathcal X$ with a proper flat morphism $f : \mathcal X \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, and a family $\Theta$ assigning to every $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent a map from pairs $(\psi, P)$, with $\psi : O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to_{\mathcal O} B$ and $P$ a Deligne datum over $B$ (a family of submodules $P.\mathrm{line}\,M \subseteq B \otimes_{\mathcal O} M$ indexed by full lattices $M$ in $K_0^2$, with invertible quotients, monotone, homothety-equivariant and nondegenerate), to the set of $B$-points $\{\varphi : \operatorname{Spec} B \to \mathcal X \mid \varphi \text{ followed by } f = \operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O \to B)\}$. Four conditions are imposed: naturality in $B$ (`hΘnat`); invariance under the twisted $\Gamma$-action `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct`, i.e. $\Theta_B(x') = \Theta_B(x)$ whenever $x'_1 = x_1 \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{-v_{\det}(\sigma\gamma)}$ and $x'_2$ is the pullback of $x_2$ along $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$, for $\gamma \in \Gamma$ (`hΘinv`); for every algebraically closed field $k$ over $\mathcal O$ with $\pi$ nilpotent and every $\psi : O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to_{\mathcal O} k$, that $\Theta_k(\psi, \cdot)$ is onto the $k$-points of $\mathcal X$ and that $\Theta_k(\psi, P) = \Theta_k(\psi, P')$ holds exactly when $(\psi,P)$ and $(\psi,P')$ are related by the twisted action of some $\gamma \in \Gamma$ (`hΘfib`); and the universal property `hΘuniv`: for every scheme $T$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ and every natural, twist-invariant family $\rho'$ into the nilpotent points of $T$ there is a natural family $u$ on the nilpotent points of $f$ with $u \circ \Theta = \rho'$, and any natural $u'$ with $u' \circ \Theta = \rho'$ agrees with $u$.
--
--   **The analytic frame.** A complete, algebraically closed valued field $C$ over $K_0$ with value group $\Gamma_0$; a commutative ring $R$ over $\mathcal O$ with $C$ an $R$-algebra and the evident scalar towers; a pseudo-uniformiser $\varpi$ of $K_0$ in $C$; the hypothesis `hF` that $(\pi, \varpi, R)$ is an adic frame, i.e. $\pi$ is irreducible, $R \to C$ is injective with image exactly the elements of valuation $\le 1$, $R$ is complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, the elements of $K_0$ of valuation $\le 1$ in $C$ are exactly those coming from $\mathcal O$, the image of $K_0$ in $C$ is closed, and $\pi$ and $\varpi.\varpi$ have the same image in $C$; an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi_0 : O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to R$; the rank-one condition `hrk` that for $x, y \in C$ with $v(x) < 1$ and $y \neq 0$ some power $v(x)^n$ is $\le v(y)$; the density condition `hval` that every nonzero $\varepsilon \in \Gamma_0$ dominates $v(y)$ for some $y \neq 0$; the exhaustion condition `hex` that every point of the Drinfeld upper half-plane $C \setminus K_0$ lies in one of the affinoids $\mathrm{affinoid}\,\varpi\,n$; and the assumption that the ring `Omega.HolRingOf` $\varpi\,\rho$ of functions holomorphic on every affinoid is a domain.
--
--   **The uniformisation of adic points.** A map $\Phi$ from adic points $x$ of the formal upper half-plane over $R$ (systems $x.\mathrm{pt}\,n$ of Deligne data over $\mathrm{modPow}\,\pi\,R\,n = R/(\pi^{n+1})$, compatible under the transition maps) to $R$-points of $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, subject to the four clauses of `hΦ`: the reduction of $\Phi x$ modulo $\pi^{n+1}$ equals the underlying morphism of $\Theta$ applied to the pair consisting of the reduction of $\psi_0$ modulo $\pi^{n+1}$ and $x.\mathrm{pt}\,n$, for every $x$ and $n$; $\Phi$ is surjective; $\Phi x = \Phi x'$ holds exactly when $x' = x.\mathrm{act}(\sigma\gamma)$ for some $\gamma \in \Gamma'$; and base change along $R \to C$ is injective on $R$-points and every $C$-point of $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ arises from an $R$-point.
--
--   **The edge charts.** The element $g_1 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ with matrix $\mathrm{diag}(\pi, 1)$ (`hg₁`); the structure morphisms $s_n : \operatorname{Spec}\bigl(O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi^{n+1})\bigr) \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ (`hsn`); and, for every $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ and every $n$, a morphism $\kappa_{h,n}$ from the spectrum of the truncation $A_n := \mathrm{chartERing}\,O^{\mathrm{nr}}\,\pi\,r / (\pi^{n+1})$ of the edge-chart ring — the localisation of $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}(\mathrm{Fin}\,2)\,O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ modulo the principal ideal generated by `edgeRel` away from the discriminant element `edgeQuot.discr` — to the pullback of $f$ along $s_n$. The chart-map law `hκ` requires: for all $h$, $n$, every $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ which is also an $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$-algebra compatibly, with $\pi$ nilpotent in $B$, every $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$-algebra map $\bar x : A_n \to B$ and all Deligne data $d, P$ over $B$: if $d$ is in edge-chart normal form, namely $d.\mathrm{line}$ of the standard full lattice is the span of $\bar x(\xi)\otimes e_0 + 1 \otimes e_1$, $d.\mathrm{line}$ of the $g_1$-translate of the standard lattice is the image under `actBaseChange` of the span of $1 \otimes e_0 + \bar x(\eta)\otimes e_1$ (where $\xi, \eta$ are the distinguished elements `chartERing.ξ` and `chartERing.η`, taken modulo $\pi^{n+1}$), and $d$ satisfies `InEdgeChart` for the pair consisting of the $g_1$-translate of the standard lattice and the standard lattice, and if $P$ is the pullback of $d$ along $h^{-1}$, then the morphism underlying $\Theta_B(\,\mathcal O\text{-to-}O^{\mathrm{nr}}\text{-structure map},\,P)$ is $\operatorname{Spec}(\bar x)$ followed by $\kappa_{h,n}$ followed by the first projection of the pullback of $f$ along $s_n$.
--
--   **The chart locus.** An open subscheme $V \subseteq \mathcal X$, a section $p \in \Gamma(V, \mathcal O_{\mathcal X})$, an element $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ and an element $t$ of the edge-chart ring, such that for every $n$ the basic open set of the image of $t$ in $A_n$ is contained in the preimage under $\kappa_{h,n}$ of the preimage of $V$ under the first projection (`ht`). Finally a subset $S \subseteq C$ characterised by `hS`: $z \in S$ if and only if $z$ lies in the Drinfeld upper half-plane (the complement of the image of $K_0$ in $C$) and, for every adic point $x$ over $R$ with $x.\mathrm{toOmega}\,C = z$ and every $n$, there are a ring homomorphism $\bar x : A_n \to R/(\pi^{n+1})$ and a Deligne datum $d$ over $R/(\pi^{n+1})$ such that $\bar x$ restricted along $O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to A_n$ is the reduction of $\psi_0$ modulo $\pi^{n+1}$, $d$ is in the edge-chart normal form described above with coordinates $\bar x(\xi), \bar x(\eta)$, the Deligne datum $x.\mathrm{pt}\,n$ is the pullback of $d$ along $h^{-1}$, and $\bar x(t)$ is a unit. Here $x.\mathrm{toOmega}\,C$ is the unique $z \in C$ with $(z,1)$ in the line of $x$ over $C$ when such a $z$ exists uniquely, and $0$ otherwise.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under these hypotheses there exists a function $F : S \to C$ with the following three properties.
--
--   First, $F$ belongs to $\mathrm{holOn}\,C\,S$: there is a sequence of pairs of polynomials over $C$, each pole-free on $S$, whose evaluations are uniformly bounded in valuation by a single element of $C$, and which converges uniformly on $S$ to $F$.
--
--   Second, $v(F(z)) \le 1$ for every $z \in S$.
--
--   Third, for every adic point $x$ over $R$, every $z \in C$ with $z = x.\mathrm{toOmega}\,C$ and $z \in S$, and under the hypothesis that the whole of $\operatorname{Spec} R$ is contained in the preimage of $V$ under the morphism $\Phi x$, the value $F(z)$ is the image under $R \to C$ of the element of $R$ obtained from $p$ by pulling back along $\Phi x$ over $V$, restricting to the top open of $\operatorname{Spec} R$, and transporting along the canonical isomorphism $\Gamma(\operatorname{Spec} R, \mathcal O) \cong R$.
--
--   This is the analytic half of the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation: regular functions on the quotient curve, pulled back through the uniformisation $\Phi$ of adic points and read as functions of the coordinate $z$ on Drinfeld's upper half-plane, are holomorphic and bounded by $1$ on the locus $S$ of points lying in a single edge chart where the localising element $t$ is invertible. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_linearPieces_le_preimage_holOn_apply_toOmega_eq_of_cerednikDrinfeld_quotient`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_linearPieces_le_preimage_holOn_apply_toOmega_eq_of_cerednikDrinfeld_quotient), where such chart loci are assembled into a covering of the upper half-plane.
